.KEY FILE/A
.BRA {
.KET }
; uterm-edit FILE -- an UP-Term window on the screen in front, running the editor on FILE. What the Directory
; Opus filetype runs on a double-click (tools/gen_dopus_filetype.py): Run >NIL: Execute UP-Term:bin/uterm-edit "%s".
; Opus has no console, so the window comes from NewShell ... FROM (the way the rig scripts and the Amarchy
; menu open one); the file and the mode go to the shell the window runs as global variables (vsh reads ENV:).
SetEnv UPTLAUNCHCMD edit
SetEnv UPTLAUNCHFILE "{FILE}"
; FRONT puts the window on the screen in front (handler/winspec.c); uterm-start ends it with EndCLI
NewShell "XCON:0/20/640/300/UP-Term/CLOSE/FRONT" FROM UP-Term:bin/uterm-start
